##:
io/error -- IoError and FileError, the error vocabulary of the io modules.

Both are predefined enums: the compiler synthesizes them, and this module is their HOME
(#574, #586). No program writes `use <io/error>` for them: `<io/contracts>` re-exports
this module and `<io/fs>` and `<io/buf>` re-export `<io/contracts>`, so `use <io/fs>`
alone brings `IoError` and `FileError` beside `File`, and `use <io/fs> as fs` puts them
behind the dot (`fs.IoError.NotFound`). `<io/files>` hands `FileError` on the same way.

IoError is the ONE channel every io contract method answers -- a read, a write, a seek,
`open()` and `close()`. FileError is what the path utilities (`stat`, `walk`, `mkdir_all`,
`remove_all`) and the `fd_*` primitives answer. The conversion between the two is
`FileError as IoError` below: a `??` in a body that answers IoError calls it, and
`e as IoError` calls it on a value.

A conversion lives in the unit that declares its TARGET, so this module also holds
`NetError as IoError`, and it imports `<net/error>` for that one name.

The variant ORDER of each is the ABI: the index is the tag the descriptor layer stores
into a Result payload, so a variant is only ever appended.
:##

use <net/error>

##:
Turns a file-system error into the one channel the io contracts answer.

Every FileError variant with no twin in IoError belongs to an open rather than to a read or
a write, so nothing a contract method can answer is lost here. IOError has already thrown
its errno away, so it collapses to Other rather than pretending to carry a number.

- Returns: The IoError that says the same thing.
:##
extend FileError as IoError:
    match self:
        FileError.NotFound -> return IoError.NotFound
        FileError.PermissionDenied -> return IoError.PermissionDenied
        FileError.AlreadyExists -> return IoError.AlreadyExists
        FileError.IsDirectory -> return IoError.IsDirectory
        FileError.DiskFull -> return IoError.DiskFull
        FileError.TooManyOpen -> return IoError.TooManyOpen
        FileError.InvalidPath -> return IoError.InvalidInput
        FileError.IOError -> return IoError.Other
        FileError.Other -> return IoError.Other

##:
Turns a socket error into the one channel the io contracts answer.

Every NetError variant with no twin in IoError belongs to a connect, a bind or a resolve,
so nothing a contract method can answer is lost here. A stream that is already connected
cannot report AddressInUse. The match names every variant, so a new variant does not
compile until it has its own row.

- Returns: The IoError that says the same thing.
:##
extend NetError as IoError:
    match self:
        NetError.ConnectionReset -> return IoError.ConnectionReset
        NetError.TimedOut -> return IoError.TimedOut
        NetError.Closed -> return IoError.Closed
        NetError.PermissionDenied -> return IoError.PermissionDenied
        NetError.TooManyOpen -> return IoError.TooManyOpen
        NetError.InvalidAddress -> return IoError.InvalidInput
        NetError.Interrupted -> return IoError.Interrupted
        NetError.ConnectionRefused -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.AddressInUse -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.AddressNotAvailable -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.NetworkUnreachable -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.HostUnreachable -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.ResolveFailed -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.MessageTooLarge -> return IoError.Other
        NetError.Other -> return IoError.Other
